<p>NOTES: Increase in 1997 Q1 net came from 11 percent rise in net interest income after provision for possible loan and lease losses, mitigated by one percent rise in non-interest expense. The primary reason for increase in net interest income is stable yields on earning assets, with lower liability costs. Net interest margin for Q1 1997 was 4.77, up from 4.61 in the year-ago quarter.</p>
